rem Minkowski Sums
rem https://projecteuler.net/problem=228
rem Count the sides of the Minkowski sum
rem of the regular polygons with from Lo
rem to Hi sides

use numbers
use sequences
use io
use cli

option Lo integer = 1864
option Hi integer = 1909

rem The sum has one side for each
rem distinct edge direction, a fraction
rem k / n of the turn. Reduced to a
rem denominator q, those are phi(q)
rem fractions, once for each q that
rem divides some n.
Q = 1 to Hi array
Phi = Q
for P in primes to Hi
  Mult = Q mod P equal 0
  Cut = Mult choose (Phi // P) 0
  Phi = Phi - Cut
end
Ns = Lo to Hi array
Rows = Q reshape Hi 1
Zero = Ns mod Rows equal 0
Divides = Zero any axis 1
Used = Phi filter Divides array
Answer = Used sum
Answer print
